@page "/docs/components/questionnaire"

<DocsPage Title="Questionnaire" Description="A multi-step questionnaire with single-choice, multiple-choice, freeform, and skippable questions.">
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-demo" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[560px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Installation" />
    <InstallationTabs Name="questionnaire" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Usage" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@DataCode" LineNumbers="true" />
    <p>Define the collection once: pass it to <code>Items</code> on <code>Questionnaire</code> so progress, actions, and shortcuts are right on the first render, then map it into the parts. <code>OnSubmit</code> receives the answers: <code>Get</code> returns an item&apos;s answer, and <code>GetAll</code> every answer of an item that takes several.</p>
    <CodeFigure Code="@MarkupCode" LineNumbers="true" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Composition" />
    <CodeFigure Code="@CompositionCode" Language="text" />
    <p>Questionnaire owns the ordered items, active item, answer state, validation, progress, and navigation. The containing page, card, dialog, or drawer owns close and cancellation behavior, persistence, transport, and branching.</p>
    <DocsHeading Title="Server Rendering" />
    <p>Pass <code>Items</code> to render the active item, progress, actions, and answer shortcuts before the items register, including during prerendering.</p>
    <DocsHeading Title="Multiple Selection" />
    <p>Use <code>Multiple</code> for an item that accepts more than one fixed answer.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-multiple" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[420px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Freeform Answer" />
    <p>Compose <code>QuestionnaireInput</code> with fixed choices when the user can provide another answer.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-freeform" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[420px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Explicit Skip" />
    <p>Add <code>QuestionnaireSkip</code> when an optional item may be intentionally left unanswered.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-skip" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Shortcuts" />
    <p>Assign a letter or number key to each answer with <code>Shortcuts</code>.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-shortcuts" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[480px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Custom Validation" />
    <p>Combine controlled navigation with your own validation to return to an invalid item and present its error.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-validation" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Controlled" />
    <p>Control the active item from host state with <code>@@bind-Item</code>, such as returning to an invalid step.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-controlled" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Resume" />
    <p>Restore a saved active item and default answers, then reset changes back to that saved state.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-resume" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Conditional Items" />
    <p>Disable items that do not apply to the user's earlier answers.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-conditional" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Navigation State" />
    <p>Read item status to opt into disabled navigation and custom action styling.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-navigation-state" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[480px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Custom Progress" />
    <p>Use the <code>Render</code> fragment of <code>QuestionnaireProgress</code> to build a custom progress indicator.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-progress" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Animated Items" />
    <p>Animate the active item while keeping progress and navigation stationary.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-animated" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[520px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Card" />
    <p>Compose Questionnaire with Card slots while keeping the question title and description semantic.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-card" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[560px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Dialog" />
    <p>Compose Questionnaire inside a Dialog while keeping cancellation and dismissal host-owned.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-dialog" Align="end" PreviewClass="min-h-[320px] p-4 sm:p-8" />
    <DocsHeading Title="Accessibility" />
    <p><code>QuestionnaireItem</code> renders a <code>fieldset</code>, and <code>QuestionnaireTitle</code> renders its <code>legend</code>. Descriptions and active errors are associated with the current item, and invalid items and answer controls expose <code>aria-invalid</code>. If the title renders something else through <code>Render</code>, give it an <code>id</code> and point the item's <code>aria-labelledby</code> at it, as the Card example does.</p>
    <p>Fixed choices preserve native radio and checkbox behavior. Progress is exposed as a named progressbar, navigation uses real buttons, and inactive items and actions are hidden and inert. Successful navigation focuses the newly active item; failed validation focuses an available answer control.</p>
    <p>Always give <code>QuestionnaireInput</code> an accessible name with a visible label, <code>aria-label</code>, or <code>aria-labelledby</code>. A placeholder is not a label.</p>
    <DocsTable>
        <table>
            <thead><tr><th>Key</th><th>Behavior</th></tr></thead>
            <tbody>
                <tr><td><code>Tab</code></td><td>Moves focus between answer controls and visible actions.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ArrowUp</code> / <code>ArrowDown</code></td><td>Moves to the previous or next answer from the item, a fixed answer, or an empty freeform input. Native radios also select it.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ArrowLeft</code></td><td>Moves to the previous item when focus is outside a radio or text field.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>ArrowRight</code></td><td>Moves to the next item when the active item is answered or skipped and focus is outside a radio or text field.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Space</code></td><td>Selects a radio, toggles a checkbox, or activates a focused action.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Enter</code></td><td>Continues from a selected choice or a selected, filled input; activates a focused action.</td></tr>
                <tr><td><code>Ctrl</code> / <code>Cmd</code> + <code>Enter</code></td><td>Validates and continues from anywhere inside the questionnaire, or submits on the last item.</td></tr>
            </tbody>
        </table>
    </DocsTable>
    <p>Shortcuts and arrow navigation pause while you type in a text field.</p>
    <DocsHeading Title="Unstyled" />
    <p>The behavior comes from the Questionnaire parts in Blazix.Primitives (<code>QuestionnaireRoot</code>, <code>QuestionnaireItem</code>, <code>QuestionnaireChoice</code>, <code>QuestionnaireChoiceInput</code>, and the rest). Use them directly with your own markup and styles.</p>
    <DocsHeading Title="RTL" />
    <p>To enable RTL support in Blazix, see the <a href="/docs/rtl">RTL configuration guide</a>.</p>
    <ComponentPreview Name="questionnaire-rtl" Direction="rtl" PreviewClass="min-h-0" />
    <DocsHeading Title="API Reference" />
    <p>Navigation components also take Button's <code>Size</code> and <code>Variant</code>, and <code>QuestionnaireActions</code> is a styled-only layout helper.</p>
    <ApiReference Name="questionnaire" />
</DocsPage>

@code {
    private const string MarkupCode = """
        <Questionnaire Items="@Definitions" OnSubmit="@HandleSubmit">
            <QuestionnaireProgress />
            @foreach (var question in Questions)
            {
                <QuestionnaireItem @key="question.Name" Name="@question.Name" Required="@question.Required">
                    <QuestionnaireTitle>@question.Prompt</QuestionnaireTitle>
                    <QuestionnaireDescription>@question.Description</QuestionnaireDescription>
                    <QuestionnaireChoices>
                        @foreach (var choice in question.Choices)
                        {
                            <QuestionnaireChoice @key="choice.Value" Value="@choice.Value">
                                <span class="font-medium">@choice.Label</span>
                                @if (choice.Description is not null)
                                {
                                    <span class="text-muted-foreground">@choice.Description</span>
                                }
                            </QuestionnaireChoice>
                        }
                        @if (question.Input is { } input)
                        {
                            <QuestionnaireInput aria-label="@input.Label" placeholder="@input.Placeholder" />
                        }
                    </QuestionnaireChoices>
                    <QuestionnaireError />
                </QuestionnaireItem>
            }
            <QuestionnaireActions>
                <QuestionnairePrevious />
                <QuestionnaireSkip />
                <QuestionnaireNext />
                <QuestionnaireSubmit />
            </QuestionnaireActions>
        </Questionnaire>
        """;

    private const string DataCode = """
        @code {
            private sealed record Choice(string Value, string Label, string? Description = null);
            private sealed record FreeformInput(string Label, string Placeholder);
            private sealed record Question(string Name, bool Required, string Prompt, string Description,
                                           Choice[] Choices, FreeformInput? Input = null);

            private static readonly Question[] Questions =
            [
                new("direction", true, "What should we prototype next?", "Choose a direction or write your own.",
                    [
                        new("delegation", "Delegation", "Show how work moves to a specialist."),
                        new("questions", "Question prompts", "Show choices while the interface waits."),
                        new("both", "Both together"),
                    ],
                    new("Another answer", "Type another answer…")),
                new("detail", false, "How much detail should it include?", "Skip this if you are not sure yet.",
                    [new("focused", "Focused"), new("complete", "Complete flow")]),
            ];

            private static readonly Blazix.Primitives.QuestionnaireItemDefinition[] Definitions =
                Questions.Select(q => new Blazix.Primitives.QuestionnaireItemDefinition(q.Name, q.Required)).ToArray();

            private void HandleSubmit(Blazix.Primitives.QuestionnaireAnswers answers)
            {
                var direction = answers.Get("direction");
            }
        }
        """;

    private const string CompositionCode = """
        Questionnaire
        ├── QuestionnaireProgress
        ├── QuestionnaireItem
        │   ├── QuestionnaireTitle
        │   ├── QuestionnaireDescription
        │   ├── QuestionnaireChoices
        │   │   ├── QuestionnaireChoice
        │   │   └── QuestionnaireInput
        │   └── QuestionnaireError
        └── QuestionnaireActions
            ├── QuestionnairePrevious
            ├── QuestionnaireSkip
            ├── QuestionnaireNext
            └── QuestionnaireSubmit
        """;
}
